# SEC-ENV-001 least-privilege env split (RT-006) — the OCI stack reads THREE
# files on the host. Copy each block below into the matching file on
# /opt/fayanms and chmod 600 every one of them. Never commit the copies.
#
# Migration from the old monolithic layout (one-time operator action BEFORE
# the next deploy — deploy.sh refuses to run without the two runtime files):
#
#   cd /opt/fayanms
#   cp .env .env.pre-rt006 && chmod 600 .env.pre-rt006   # backup, review, then shred
#   # keep in .env:      the "FILE: /opt/fayanms/.env" block below (host-side
#   #                    interpolation ONLY — delete every secret line from it)
#   # move to .env.app:  the "FILE: /opt/fayanms/.env.app" block below
#   # move to .env.worker: the "FILE: /opt/fayanms/.env.worker" block below
#   chmod 600 /opt/fayanms/.env /opt/fayanms/.env.app /opt/fayanms/.env.worker
#
# Zone contract (ownership table — SEC-ENV-001, enforced by the boot policy):
#   host .env        interpolation values only (images, ports, domains, DB URL,
#                    POSTGRES_PASSWORD) — compose ${VAR:?} reads THIS file;
#   .env.app         app zone: session secret, config-encryption KEK, CONTROL
#                    keypair, proxy/login knobs — attached to `app` ONLY;
#   .env.worker      worker zone: WORKER keypair, vault credentials, CA pin —
#                    attached to `worker` ONLY;
#   postgres / migrate / caddy receive NO env_file at all (their environment
#   is interpolated from the host .env in compose.yml).

# ===== FILE: /opt/fayanms/.env =====
# Host-side — compose --env-file interpolation ONLY. Values compose.yml
# interpolates at parse time. NO runtime secret material: no NEXTAUTH_SECRET,
# no KEK, no keypairs, no vault entries — those live in the per-service
# files below.

FAYANMS_IMAGE=ghcr.io/faya-corporation/fayanms:REPLACE_WITH_FULL_COMMIT_SHA
FAYANMS_WORKER_IMAGE=ghcr.io/faya-corporation/fayanms-worker:REPLACE_WITH_FULL_COMMIT_SHA
FAYANMS_MIGRATOR_IMAGE=ghcr.io/faya-corporation/fayanms-migrator:REPLACE_WITH_FULL_COMMIT_SHA

FAYANMS_TLS_DOMAIN=nms-staging.example.com
# F-026: SITE_URL is a RUNTIME env (NOT build-time). Host-side values take
# effect on the published GHCR images WITHOUT any rebuild — the origin is
# resolved per request by src/lib/brand/site-url.ts. localhost/*.local are
# rejected in production.
SITE_URL=https://nms-staging.example.com
NEXTAUTH_URL=https://nms-staging.example.com

POSTGRES_PASSWORD=SET_ON_HOST_ONLY
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://fayanms:SET_ON_HOST_ONLY@postgres:5432/fayanms

# Optional operator controls. Defaults are conservative.
FAYANMS_HTTP_PORT=80
FAYANMS_HTTPS_PORT=443
FAYANMS_BACKUP_DIR=/opt/fayanms/backups
# GRAFANA_ADMIN_PASSWORD=...   # only when compose.monitoring.yml is deployed

# ===== FILE: /opt/fayanms/.env.app =====
# App zone — attached to the `app` service ONLY.
# Zone contract (docs/deploy/env.app.production.example is the full reference):
#   ✓ app zone      session secrets, the config-encryption KEK, the CONTROL
#                   service-identity keypair, proxy/login knobs.
#   ✗ never here    FAYANMS_VAULT_* device credentials (the WORKER resolves
#                   them), FAYANMS_WEBAPI_CA_PEM, NEXT_BASE_URL /
#                   SELF_BASE_URL. DATABASE_URL is composed by compose from
#                   the host-side POSTGRES_PASSWORD above.

# Session secret (openssl rand -hex 32). Required, >= 32 chars.
NEXTAUTH_SECRET=SET_ON_HOST_ONLY

# Configuration-encryption KEK: 64 hex chars. Losing it = losing every
# config-snapshot backup; back it up OFF-BOX. NEVER leaves the app.
FAYANMS_CONFIG_ENC_KEY=SET_64_HEX_CHARS_ON_HOST_ONLY
FAYANMS_CONFIG_ENC_KEY_ID=oci-staging-k1

# Service identity — CONTROL keypair (EdDSA-only production, RECOMMENDED).
# Generate with `bun run keys:service` (one run per keypair — the WORKER
# env file holds the OTHER keypair):
#   FAYANMS_SERVICE_PRIVATE_KEY = CONTROL private key (the app mints
#                                 control-plane tokens it sends to the worker)
#   FAYANMS_SERVICE_PUBLIC_KEYS = WORKER public keys (comma-separated)
FAYANMS_SERVICE_PRIVATE_KEY=SET_ON_HOST_ONLY
FAYANMS_SERVICE_PUBLIC_KEYS=SET_ON_HOST_ONLY
# Legacy symmetric plane (migration/legacy modes ONLY — leave empty for
# the recommended EdDSA-only configuration).
# FAYANMS_SERVICE_SECRET=
# FAYANMS_SERVICE_SECRETS=
# No FAYANMS_SERVICE_JWT_KID knob exists (that is deliberate): service tokens are trusted by signature under configured keys; no kid selection exists.

# API rate gate + login abuse control (app-zone knobs).
FAYANMS_TRUST_PROXY_HOPS=1
# The OCI compose topology runs the app behind the Caddy TLS proxy, which
# APPENDS the real client address to X-Forwarded-For — declare it (wave-11
# contract: the startup policy REFUSES a production boot when hops > 0 is
# undeclared; a direct-published topology must use
# FAYANMS_TRUST_PROXY_HOPS=0 instead).
FAYANMS_PUBLIC_PROXY=true
# FAYANMS_LOGIN_WINDOW_SECONDS=300
# FAYANMS_LOGIN_MAX_ATTEMPTS_PER_SOURCE=10
# FAYANMS_LOGIN_MAX_ATTEMPTS_PER_ACCOUNT=30

# Bearer token for internal Prometheus scraping of the app's /api/metrics.
# Never expose it in public URLs or logs. NOTE (wave-12, audit 18-b): this
# placeholder is on the startup policy's known-bad list — a production boot
# REFUSES while it still reads SET_ON_HOST_ONLY. Replace it on the host:
#   openssl rand -hex 32
FAYANMS_METRICS_TOKEN=SET_ON_HOST_ONLY

# ===== FILE: /opt/fayanms/.env.worker =====
# Worker zone — attached to the `worker` service ONLY.
# Zone contract (docs/deploy/env.worker.production.example is the full
# reference):
#   ✓ worker zone   the WORKER service-identity keypair, the CONTROL public
#                   keys, device vault credentials (FAYANMS_VAULT_*), the
#                   SFOS WebAPI CA pin.
#   ✗ never here    NEXTAUTH_SECRET / NEXTAUTH_URL, FAYANMS_CONFIG_ENC_KEY(+_ID)
#                   (the KEK never leaves the app), POSTGRES_PASSWORD /
#                   DATABASE_URL (the worker never touches PostgreSQL).

# Service identity — WORKER keypair (the app env file holds the OTHER
# keypair):
#   FAYANMS_SERVICE_PRIVATE_KEY = WORKER private key (the worker signs the
#                                 persistence-API tokens the app verifies)
#   FAYANMS_SERVICE_PUBLIC_KEYS = CONTROL public keys (comma-separated)
FAYANMS_SERVICE_PRIVATE_KEY=SET_ON_HOST_ONLY
FAYANMS_SERVICE_PUBLIC_KEYS=SET_ON_HOST_ONLY
# Legacy symmetric plane (migration/legacy modes ONLY).
# FAYANMS_SERVICE_SECRET=

# Device vault credentials — one env entry per vault reference
# (vault://ssh/network-admin → FAYANMS_VAULT_SSH_NETWORK_ADMIN). Keep device
# secret values outside Git; resolve them on the worker using the
# repository's secretRef contract.
# FAYANMS_VAULT_SSH_NETWORK_ADMIN=SET_ON_HOST_ONLY
# FAYANMS_VAULT_WEBAPI_SOPHOS_HQ=SET_ON_HOST_ONLY
FAYANMS_VAULT_PROVIDER=env

# SFOS WebAPI TLS pin (fail-closed; optional extra CA for private chains).
# FAYANMS_WEBAPI_CA_PEM=

# Bearer token for internal Prometheus scraping of the worker's /api/metrics.
# Same contract as the app zone above (wave-12, audit 18-b): the placeholder
# is on the startup policy's known-bad list — replace it on the host
# (openssl rand -hex 32) before the first production boot.
FAYANMS_METRICS_TOKEN=SET_ON_HOST_ONLY
